From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RicemanRhys <176650384+RicemanRhys@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:29:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Local-only: xbox_d3d8 baked draws: a UP draw captured once
 and drawn again from what it bound (perf only, identical output)

- d3d8_BakeCapture / d3d8_DrawBaked (d3d8_internal.h, D3D8Baked): the next
  UP draw is captured as it is made, after its translation: the vertex and
  pixel shaders, input layout, blend, depth-stencil and rasterizer objects,
  stencil reference, samplers, viewport, the constant buffers bound, the
  fixed-function transform and lighting constants and the pixel constants
  as uploaded (into a per-frame bake memory, identical blocks shared), and
  where the rings hold its vertices and indices. d3d8_DrawBaked draws it
  again with the caller's texture views and program constants (or the
  fixed-function matrices given again: ff_xf_matrices, the ordinary path's
  own code), binding only what differs from what is bound. xbox_d3d8's D3D8
  state is left as it was; what the buffers hold is kept true (the held
  copies updated, or the next ordinary draw uploads again).
- Captures stay valid while d3d8_bake_gen and the rings' generation are
  unchanged: the VSH cache's eviction, the combiners' LRU eviction, the
  fixed-function pixel shaders' eviction and a full sampler cache bump it.
- Blend, depth-stencil and rasterizer objects are cached by description
  (64 each) instead of released and created again at every change, so a
  capture can hold them; the runtime returns the same object for the same
  description, so the same objects are bound as before.
- With D3D11.1 constant-buffer offsets, a captured program draw's 192
  registers go into a 32 MB constants ring (each at its own offset, the
  block before reused while they haven't changed), and a baked draw whose
  registers are unchanged binds the capture's block; a moved one writes a
  new block. Without offsets: g_vsh_cb as before.
- d3d8_BakeReset (a capturing frame's start): the bake memory reused, and
  the vertex, index and constant rings started over when they may not hold
  the frame (the last frame's bytes, a quarter more and 1 MB): a ring that
  started over in the middle of a frame took the captures before it with it.
- tests/d3d8_smoke/test_a8.c: stubs for the new symbols it doesn't link.

For twoc's sub-frames (each recorded frame drawn up to four times; twoc's
RECOMP_D3D_BRIDGE_BAKE). Under the twoc notes' 18.63 rule refinement
(perf-only changes in xbox_d3d8, local, never pushed); twoc notes 18.90.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
